---
import Page from "../layouts/Page.astro";
import InfoRow from "../components/InfoRow.astro";

const unpublished = ["Google Chrome", "Spotify", "Google Drive", "AnyDesk"];
const installers = ["Zoom", "Microsoft Teams", "Google Drive", "OneDrive", "Tailscale", "TeamViewer"];
---

<Page
  title="How SettleIn checks every app"
  description="SettleIn checks the signature, notarization and checksum of every app before it installs."
>
  <div class="page-head">
    <h1>How SettleIn checks every app</h1>
    <p>
      Every app comes straight from its own developer, and SettleIn checks it before it installs. If a
      check fails, SettleIn refuses that app and tells you which one and why.
    </p>
  </div>
  <div class="info-list">
    <InfoRow icon="pen" title="Developer ID signature">
      <p>Every download must be signed with a valid Developer ID.</p>
      <p>A missing or broken signature means SettleIn refuses the app.</p>
    </InfoRow>
    <InfoRow icon="shield" title="Apple notarization">
      <p>Apple must have notarized the download.</p>
      <p>If it hasn’t, SettleIn refuses it.</p>
    </InfoRow>
    <InfoRow icon="hash" title="Checksum">
      <p>When the catalog lists a SHA-256 checksum, the download must match it exactly.</p>
      <p>These apps publish no checksum, so they rely on the signature and notarization checks:</p>
      <ul class="chips">
        {unpublished.map((name) => <li>{name}</li>)}
      </ul>
    </InfoRow>
    <InfoRow icon="lock" title="macOS checks again">
      <p>SettleIn keeps the quarantine flag on every app it installs.</p>
      <p>That way macOS runs its own check the first time you open each one.</p>
    </InfoRow>
    <InfoRow icon="box" title="Installers stay Apple’s">
      <p>These apps come as installer packages.</p>
      <p>SettleIn checks them, then opens them in Apple’s Installer for you to click through:</p>
      <ul class="chips">
        {installers.map((name) => <li>{name}</li>)}
      </ul>
    </InfoRow>
    <InfoRow icon="list" title="One source for the list">
      <p>The app reads its catalog only from <span class="domain">settlein.dev</span>.</p>
    </InfoRow>
    <InfoRow icon="trash" title="Clean removal">
      <p>When you uninstall an app, SettleIn deletes only the files the catalog lists for it.</p>
      <p>Removing an installer-package app asks for your admin password once.</p>
    </InfoRow>
  </div>
</Page>
